From f129d0ef4c282ec03c10d42ea95074422d1b53cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:19:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] vfs: folio reservation: use div_u64() for the sectors per
 replica

disk_reservation.sectors is a u64; dividing it with a plain / makes gcc
emit a libgcc call on 32 bit, which the kernel doesn't provide. The DKMS
build on armv7 fails at modpost:

  ERROR: modpost: "__aeabi_uldivmod" [src/fs/bcachefs/bcachefs.ko] undefined!

With this the module links on armv7 (7.2.7, C-only build) and loads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 fs/vfs/pagecache.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/vfs/pagecache.c b/fs/vfs/pagecache.c
index 221db88be4..249010f3d8 100644
--- a/fs/vfs/pagecache.c
+++ b/fs/vfs/pagecache.c
@@ -535,7 +535,7 @@ static ssize_t __bch2_folio_reservation_get(struct bch_fs *c,
 					      res->disk.nr_replicas,
 					      partial ? BCH_DISK_RESERVATION_PARTIAL : 0));
 
-		unsigned got = disk_res.r.sectors / disk_res.r.nr_replicas;
+		unsigned got = div_u64(disk_res.r.sectors, disk_res.r.nr_replicas);
 		if (unlikely(got < last - first)) {
 			/*
 			 * Make sure to get a reservation that's aligned to the
